<Base lang="en-US" pageType="CollectionPage" title="Martín Fierro for Students: Canto-by-Canto Study Guides" description="Study Martín Fierro in English with canto summaries, original Spanish excerpts, vocabulary, themes, characters and comprehension questions.">
<main class="students"><nav class="crumb"><a href="/en/">English edition</a> / <a href="/en/library/">Popular library</a> / Study guides</nav><header><p class="eyebrow">OPEN STUDY LIBRARY · ENGLISH STUDY RESOURCES</p><h1>Martín Fierro <em>for Students</em></h1><p class="intro">Learn the story canto by canto without losing contact with José Hernández’s original Spanish words. Each published guide includes the plot, major voices, selected authentic verses, literary themes and questions for reflection.</p></header><section><h2>Part One — El gaucho Martín Fierro (1872)</h2><div class="cards">{lessons.map(x=><article><p class="chapter">CANTO {x.n}</p><h3><a href={`/en/students/canto-${x.n}/`}>{x.title}</a></h3><p>{x.desc}</p><a href={`/en/students/canto-${x.n}/`}>Read the study guide ↗</a> · <a href={`/leer/ida/${x.n}/`} lang="es">Original poem</a></article>)}</div><p class="note">All thirteen cantos of the 1872 first part now have individual study guides. Additional cantos will be linked only when their guides have been completed and verified against the original corpus.</p></section><section><h2>Part Two — La vuelta de Martín Fierro (1879)</h2><div class="cards"><article><p class="chapter">CANTO I</p><h3><a href="/en/students/vuelta-canto-1/">The Return Begins: Fierro Sings Again</a></h3><p>The narrator resumes his song and claims a right to be heard.</p><a href="/en/students/vuelta-canto-1/">Read the study guide ↗</a> · <a href="/leer/vuelta/1/" lang="es">Original poem</a></article><article><p class="chapter">CANTO II</p><h3><a href="/en/students/vuelta-canto-2/">Fierro and Cruz Arrive Beyond the Frontier</a></h3><p>Arrival at an Indigenous settlement, suspicion and captivity.</p><a href="/en/students/vuelta-canto-2/">Read the study guide ↗</a> · <a href="/leer/vuelta/2/" lang="es">Original poem</a></article><article><p class="chapter">CANTO III</p><h3><a href="/en/students/vuelta-canto-3/">Two Years Apart: Fierro and Cruz Survive Captivity</a></h3><p>Separation, shelter and hunting for survival.</p><a href="/en/students/vuelta-canto-3/">Read the study guide ↗</a> · <a href="/leer/vuelta/3/" lang="es">Original poem</a></article><article><p class="chapter">CANTO IV</p><h3><a href="/en/students/vuelta-canto-4/">Horsemen, Raids and Fierro’s Prejudices</a></h3><p>Riding skills, raid descriptions and racist stereotypes.</p><a href="/en/students/vuelta-canto-4/">Read the study guide ↗</a> · <a href="/leer/vuelta/4/" lang="es">Original poem</a></article><article><p class="chapter">CANTO V</p><h3><a href="/en/students/vuelta-canto-5/">The Spoils of Raids and Women’s Labor</a></h3><p>Contradictions in Fierro’s descriptions of life beyond the frontier.</p><a href="/en/students/vuelta-canto-5/">Read the study guide ↗</a> · <a href="/leer/vuelta/5/" lang="es">Original poem</a></article></div><p class="note">The first five cantos of the 1879 sequel have verified guides. The remaining 28 sequel guides will be added as they are researched.</p></section><section class="feature"><h2>Read across the whole poem</h2><p><a href="/en/library/old-vizcacha-vs-martin-fierro/">Old Vizcacha versus Martín Fierro</a> compares different approaches to life and morality using original passages from the sequel’s Cantos XV and XXXII. The <a href="/en/martin-fierro-advice-to-his-sons/">complete advice to his sons</a> is also available with English explanations.</p><p><a href="/en/martin-fierro-summary/">Story summary</a> · <a href="/en/characters/">Main characters</a> · <a href="/en/library/themes-and-analysis/">Themes and analysis</a> · <a href="/en/magazine/frontier-forts/">Frontier history</a></p></section></main>
